sed same-path receipt for the exact bundle. The live child is ALREADY_APPLIED only with a successful rolling terminal artifact plus matching live verification event and passed run closure. Resume the first absent child; conflicts or open blockers are INDETERMINATE."},"execute":{"candidate_reconciliation":{"absorb/supersede/already-promoted":"Re-observe the exact frozen target bundle and current same-path registered verification. Matching checkpoint evidence is ALREADY_APPLIED; absent checkpoint with unchanged proof is NOT_APPLIED; proof drift is INDETERMINATE.","promote":"Require the approved discovery-promotion-lifecycle child terminal artifact and matching registered target bundle/same-path verification. Exact proof is ALREADY_APPLIED; no child evidence is NOT_APPLIED; partial or conflicting promotion evidence is INDETERMINATE.","remain-discovery/quarantine":"Require the original discovery bytes and deterministic retained checkpoint row; exact row is ALREADY_APPLIED, absence is NOT_APPLIED, and discovery drift is INDETERMINATE."},"effect_identity":"approval receipt id plus manifest hash plus repository/candidate/registry snapshot plus fixed active-index target","prepare":"Persist and consume the approval receipt, numeric N/P UnitBudget, deterministic per-candidate child ids, expected checkpoint path/content progression, original discovery hashes, and expected active-index bytes before the first candidate.","resume_rule":"Resume from the first candidate lacking exact semantic proof/checkpoint. A checkpoint alone cannot override missing child proof, and child proof after a crash prevents duplicate promotion."},"execute-rolling":{"attempt_rule":"At most six deterministic attempts; never create a new invocation directory or repeat an already proved candidate effect after a crash.","effect_identity":"parent effect id plus approved policy hash plus fixed active-index target plus deterministic attempt ids 1..6","prepare":"Use effect-derived attempt directories rather than random UUIDs. For each attempt, persist the fresh audit hash, applied policy rows, N/P numeric budget, child ids, checkpoint target, and expected active-index bytes before execution.","reconciliation":"Reconcile each attempt through its audit, candidate child proofs/checkpoint, active index, and stable post-audit. Candidate-set arrival with no semantic decision change closes that attempt as superseded-by-next-attempt; changed existing disposition, non-retain arrival, target drift, or allowlist drift is INDETERMINATE and stops."},"validate":{"effect_class":"OBSERVATION","effect_identity":"manifest canonical hash plus current repository/candidate/registry hashes","reconciliation":"Replay complete schema, snapshot, disposition, target bundle, and approval checks; return typed validity without mutation."}},"policy_sha256":"d535ca33ab45c52ac9afb05f6a50121fff55a938845f97c12350954ffbe8a30c","required_clause_ids":["11f4df559105ce32c8f15f7f5d5fceeef46b580fd3fd7ada7b0e0d6608625b03","232d8d063bd34eabbb0c74249f2d921b2412aa5bdd80da7d7ec54de557fe065a","260338add766bde68fd01dd52ff89c11a8c6f3f7b5ffc37befe6e59499935fa9","26443ffc0656d8a1c27095f6b21934ab1497ce16533c1da57055c5f8adcd3d61","48acf238557a69113d8df0d64af72c51fbd99c760fdfe04125b768805afb20dd","4b87a38b27635162d563e34d3e1a0c0fe3ca03bc99b3ce6f374a362bd7d8756a","55f710d9ee203f491eb7dd5fe7644b5b410de5a5da6dcf2caeb71bdcce3dd3f9","5c2319a4739722ab7540131145a003aa9c47811d425d06e27ff1cfbdd6416f87","6989e6672fa7c46896cfdaf483e0377197c522402b2d8e78bbf577535a768e93","a2da6ecc1b3e6740a797951b9adc4355000bb774efed29b816bd8957debb9660","a81025916bbc6c78394971dd6432eb21c4cff9eb5235d36e3ef31720048ddf1a","ab2aedc7a6e006aaa1a6391e22c11ab3561e1abe45f07202be1c331ba7f045ea","b5e5556dcd8a44a0b1aaf2e96ab7b0087ee41443112c25f97573951526fcfc06","de23b7fd394f6eebb432717fa9d9aa8f186a4cfd3577a3d0a3dbec6112bf5bf2","ee912a61757ba8aa71bb273877540652bd05ff87618671021a6b1e2093106931","ef4df0305c22cce1ca0f707ba91e31c3b2d98d92274f7b6f31659fa4ae7b2edd","ef69e